## Ⅴ. BUSINESS MODELS (Value Layer)

How value flows through the organism.

### Client Model

```
CLIENT_MODEL:
    1. Client connects (instant)
    2. Organism instantiates copy (same architecture)
    3. Internal teams spawn (per-client)
    4. Data flows:
        Client → Ingestion → Compression → Storage
                                        → Dashboard (client view)
                                        → Founder (master view)
    
    500 CLIENTS = SAME MODEL × 500
    NO NEW ARCHITECTURE NEEDED
```

### Revenue Model

```
REVENUE_MODEL:
    Subscription per client
    Value = φ × (data_organized + insights_generated + time_saved)
    
    Scales with φ:
    - More data → more compression opportunities
    - More patterns → more valuable insights
    - More time → better predictions
```

### Scaling Model

```
SCALING_MODEL:
    Memory: O(log n) per client (φ-compression)
    Compute: O(1) per operation (same architecture)
    Time: O(1) to onboard (instant instantiation)
    
    THE ARCHITECTURE DOESN'T CHANGE.
    ONLY INSTANCES MULTIPLY.
```

